// Frozen native briefs retain their original exact bytes. This legacy format
// is only a compatibility comparison, never the instructions for new work.
const nativeS6LegacyProfessionalFormat = "\nUse Claude Code native worktree isolation from Main HEAD %s. Save the following professional JSON files relative to your actual worktree; do not write these drafts into Main. Plan before implementation; save does not activate anything. Implement, self-test, commit only actual TASK products and save Result. Keep these private professional files out of Git; do not force-add them. Return this exact brief reference %s and the absolute path to your Result. Do not run workspace launch, agent-begin or task-complete.\n\nPlan: %s\n```json\n{\"objective\":null,\"planned_paths\":[],\"assertion_checks\":[{\"assertion\":null,\"oracle\":null,\"done_when_indexes\":[]}],\"risks_blockers\":[]}\n```\nPlan fields are objective, planned_paths, assertion_checks and risks_blockers only. Plan.risks_blockers is an array of strings. Registered dependencies are system facts, not a private Plan question. Each assertion has assertion, oracle and done_when_indexes (zero-based indices into Done when). Cover each required condition.\n\nResult: %s\n```json\n{\"summary\":null,\"assertion_evidence\":[{\"assertion\":null,\"oracle\":null,\"evidence_refs\":[]}],\"risks_blockers\":[],\"scope_deviations\":[],\"closing_assessment\":{\"disposition\":null,\"conditions\":[{\"done_when_index\":0,\"judgment\":null,\"plan_assertion_indexes\":[],\"rationale\":null}]}}\n```\nResult fields are summary, assertion_evidence, risks_blockers, scope_deviations and closing_assessment only. Result has no dependencies field. Use exactly the shown field names; no extra nested fields. Each assertion_evidence item has assertion and oracle copied verbatim from its plan assertion, plus nonempty evidence_refs containing exact existing file paths relative to your worktree, within this TASK write scope or its listed Read paths. These are file references: omit line numbers, fragments, descriptions, command text and output. Put commands, outputs and observations in summary or closing rationale; cite their actual evidence file only when it exists within the allowed scope. Result.risks_blockers and Result.scope_deviations are arrays of strings. Any unresolved Result risk/blocker or scope deviation prevents completion/integration; report real ones honestly. Put non-blocking context, scope limitations and resolved-risk explanations in summary/closing rationale, without hiding unfinished obligations. Replace nulls with your own professional answers; do not copy placeholder values. closing_assessment has disposition (complete/incomplete/blocked) and conditions; each condition has done_when_index, judgment (satisfied/incomplete/blocked), plan_assertion_indexes and rationale. Include real self-check commands/results in summary. When blocked, also state the actual blocker and unfinished work directly in your native return. A real blocker is an honest handoff, never a fabricated PASS.\n"

func nativeS6LegacyProfessionalInstructions(base, brief, plan, result string) string {
	return fmt.Sprintf(nativeS6LegacyProfessionalFormat, base, brief, plan, result)
}

